description:
Add the static UI scaffolding for attachments: CSS classes and HTML elements.

**What:** Add CSS and HTML needed by all attachment JS to reference; no JS logic.

**Files:** web/style.css, web/index.html

**Algorithm:**
1. web/style.css — add these classes:
   `.attachment-preview` { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; min-height: 0; }
   `.attachment-preview-item` { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; background: #f0f0f0; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 6px; font-size: 0.8em; }
   `.attachment-preview-item .remove-btn` { background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; font-size: 1em; padding: 0 2px; }
   `.message-attachments` { margin-top: 6px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
   `.attachment-link` { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; text-decoration: none; color: #0066cc; font-size: 0.85em; }
   `.attachment-link:hover` { text-decoration: underline; }
   `.attachment-size` { color: #888; font-size: 0.85em; }

2. web/index.html — inside the `.compose` div (which contains `#compose-body` and `#send-btn`):
   - Before the `<textarea>`, add: `<div id="attachment-preview" class="attachment-preview"></div>`
   - After `#send-btn`, add: `<button id="attach-btn" type="button" title="Attach file" aria-label="Attach file">📎</button>`
   - After the compose div, add: `<input type="file" id="file-input" style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">`

**Defensive rules:**
- Hidden file input must have `aria-hidden="true"` (it is not navigable).
- Attach button has `type="button"` to avoid form submit.
- All IDs must match exactly what JS in later beads will reference: `file-input`, `attach-btn`, `attachment-preview`.

**Tests:** Visual check: no layout shift when preview div is empty (min-height 0); attach button appears next to send.
